    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "REA Hynes are delighted to bring to the market Mount Vista, a substantial four-bedroom detached family home set on a generous c.0.57-acre (0.23 hectare) site in the highly sought-after area of Creaghduff, Coosan, Athlone. Ideally positioned directly opposite Coosan National School, this impressive property offers an excellent combination of spacious family accommodation, extensive private grounds, excellent outdoor living space and a convenient location.\nExtending to approximately 157 sq.m. (1,690 sq.ft.), Mount Vista provides well-proportioned and versatile accommodation throughout, making it an ideal home for families seeking space both inside and out.\nOn entering, the bright entrance hall leads to the heart of the home. The generous sitting room is a particular feature, offering an impressive and versatile space for both family living and entertaining. Excellent proportions, large windows and an abundance of natural light create a warm and welcoming atmosphere, while the attractive glazed timber double doors provide an appealing architectural feature and allow light to flow between the adjoining reception areas. The open connection with the dining area creates an excellent sense of space and makes this a particularly practical setting for both everyday family life and larger gatherings.\nThe living accommodation also benefits from patio doors opening directly from the living room onto the patio, creating a seamless connection between the house and gardens. During the warmer months, the patio provides a natural extension to the living and entertaining space, making it particularly convenient for alfresco dining, family gatherings and enjoying the extensive grounds.\nThe kitchen/breakfast room is bright, well proportioned and highly functional, with a good range of built-in units providing ample storage and preparation space, together with a useful breakfast counter. Two windows overlook the rear gardens and grounds, while the direct connection to the dining area makes entertaining and family meals particularly convenient. The accommodation is further complemented by a utility room, cloakroom and WC.\nThere are four well proportioned bedrooms, including a principal bedroom with ensuite, together with a well-appointed main bathroom. The bedroom accommodation offers excellent flexibility for a growing family, guest accommodation or those requiring space for a home office.\nExternally, Mount Vista occupies a substantial c.0.57-acre site with private, mature gardens and considerable space surrounding the property. A particularly appealing feature is the privacy afforded by the grounds, with the house not overlooked, creating a peaceful and secure environment for family life and offering added reassurance for those with young children or pets.\nThe gardens have been thoughtfully positioned to make the most of the property's sunny aspect, with the lower patio providing a wonderful sun trap and the orientation of the house and gardens maximising the available sunlight throughout the day. Together with the direct connection from the living room, this creates a superb outdoor setting for relaxing, entertaining and dining during the summer months.\nThe property is approached via a substantial driveway providing parking for at least three cars, with the double entrance/access arrangement offering additional flexibility. A large detached double garage, measuring approximately 5.50m x 5.38m, provides valuable space for vehicles, storage, workshop use or hobbies. In addition, the garage benefits from an enclosed and lockable brick-built storage shed, providing particularly secure additional storage space.\nThe location is a key attraction. Situated in the popular and well-established Coosan area, Mount Vista is directly opposite Coosan National School and is within easy reach of Coosan Point, Lough Ree and Athlone town centre. The area offers an appealing blend of a pleasant semi-rural setting while remaining within convenient reach of Athlone and the wider Midlands.\nMount Vista represents an excellent opportunity to acquire a substantial detached family home on a generous and exceptionally private site in a highly desirable Coosan location. With its well proportioned accommodation, four bedrooms, extensive gardens, sunny outdoor spaces, detached double garage, secure additional storage and excellent accessibility, the property offers considerable appeal for families seeking a home with space, privacy and excellent potential.\nViewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate the generous accommodation, private setting, outdoor living space and many possibilities this fine family home has to offer.\nFor further information or to arrange a viewing, please contact REA Hynes on 090 647 3838 or email info@hynes.ie.\n\nDISCLAIMER: Please note that while every effort has been made to ensure the accuracy of the property details, they are intended as a general guide and do not constitute part of an offer or contract. Prospective purchasers are advised to verify all particulars independently before making any decisions. \n\nOutside\nExternally, Mount Vista is set on a generous and beautifully established site of approximately 0.23 hectares (0.57 acres), offering an excellent degree of space, privacy and mature landscaping. The grounds are well stocked with mature trees, established shrubbery and colourful seasonal flowers, creating an attractive and welcoming setting around the property. The gardens are particularly private, with the house not overlooked, providing a peaceful and secluded environment which is ideal for family life and offers an added sense of security for young children and pets. The gardens provide plenty of room for outdoor entertaining, family activities and further landscaping, while the mature planting adds considerably to the overall sense of privacy and seclusion. A particular feature of the property is the double entrance, providing excellent access to the grounds and offering considerable flexibility for parking, vehicles, trailers or additional outdoor storage. The generous driveway provides parking for at least three cars, while the layout of the grounds allows for further flexibility depending on the needs of the occupier. The property also benefits from a substantial detached double garage, measuring approximately 5.50m x 5.38m, which provides generous space for two vehicles together with excellent additional storage or workshop potential. Adjoining the garage is a separate enclosed and lockable brick-built shed, providing secure additional storage space and further enhancing the property's practicality. The outdoor living space is further complemented by a large patio area accessed directly from the living room through patio doors, creating a natural extension to the home's living and entertaining space during the warmer months. The patio is ideally suited to alfresco dining, outdoor entertaining and relaxing with family and friends. The lower patio is a particular feature, enjoying a sunny aspect and acting as a wonderful sun trap, while the orientation of the house and gardens has been carefully positioned to make the most of the available sunlight. Overall, the extensive and private grounds, mature planting, sunny patios, double entrance, generous parking and excellent garage and secure storage facilities combine to make the outside space a particularly attractive and versatile feature of Mount Vista."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "REA Hynes are delighted to present Mount Vista, a substantial four-bedroom detached family home set on an impressive c.0.57-acre private site in the highly sought-after Coosan area of Athlone. Ideally located directly opposite Coosan National School, this well-proportioned home offers excellent family accommodation, beautifully established gardens and superb outdoor living space. A private, non-overlooked setting, sunny patios, detached double garage, secure storage and parking for at least three cars further enhance the property's appeal. Viewing is highly recommended to appreciate the space, setting and potential on offer.\n\nProperty Features\nSubstantial four-bedroom detached family home\nGenerous c.0.57-acre (0.23 hectare) private site\nApprox. 157 sq.m. (1,690 sq.ft.)\nDirectly opposite Coosan National School\nPrivate, non-overlooked gardens\nMature, beautifully established grounds\nExcellent sunny aspect with lower patio enjoying a sun-trap\nPatio doors from living room to patio — ideal for alfresco dining and entertaining\nSpacious sitting room with glazed timber double doors\nBright kitchen/breakfast room with breakfast counter\nPrincipal bedroom with ensuite\nUtility room, cloakroom and WC\nDetached double garage approx. 5.50m x 5.38m\nSecure enclosed and lockable brick-built shed adjoining garage\nDouble entrance with excellent access to grounds\nDriveway providing parking for at least three cars\nExcellent potential for family living, hobbies and storage\nConvenient to Coosan Point, Lough Ree and Athlone town centre"
      },
